# COM: incremental must NOT report it as a new gain.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/gap-fill/incremental/new_coverage.csv --check-prefix=NO_BASELINE_GAIN
# NO_BASELINE_GAIN-NOT: /AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp,160,

# COM: The same coverage gaps reported by incremental (GAP_CSV) must be reported as
# COM: all-points-uncovered by target-lines when fed as target lines.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/target_lines/target_lines_uncovered.csv --check-prefix=TARGET_CSV
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: file,line,text
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,211,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,222,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,581,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,590,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,680,

# COM: AMDGPUAliasAnalysis.cpp:103 is fully covered (covered in line_coverage_summary.csv) but
# COM: present in the sample target CSV, so target-lines must filter it out of the report.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/target_lines/target_lines_uncovered.csv --check-prefix=TARGET_CSV_NOT
# TARGET_CSV_NOT-NOT: /AMDGPUAliasAnalysis.cpp,103,

# COM: None of these real coverage gaps are an assert/report_fatal_error/... call, a
# COM: multi-line control-flow header, or a blank/brace-only line, so gap-pruner must
# COM: leave every one of them in place.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/target_lines/target_lines_pruned.csv --check-prefix=PRUNED_CSV
# PRUNED_CSV-DAG: file,line,text
# PRUNED_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,211,
# PRUNED_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,222,
# PRUNED_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,581,
# PRUNED_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,590,
# PRUNED_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,680,

# COM: Real batch reduction on the first gap-fill row (manually confirmed with llvmorg-22.1.8 sancov build).
# RUN: %reduce batch-from-coverage --gap-fill-dir %t/gap-fill -n 1 --corpus-dir %S/fixtures/coverage-new-tests --llvm-bin %llvm-sancov-bin --instrumented-bin-dir %llvm-sancov-bin --pipeline llvm_reduce_ir
